  "query_preview": "..Ahh the monsoon. It never fails that what looks \nlike an active day 24 to 48 hours out in the model world ends \nup to be much less. Today is a good example as drier air has \npunched in from the east with no storms on radar as of 230 pm. \nThe CAMs are also been struggling today. Although its been a \nslow start to the convection, still looking at widely scattered \nstorms developing in the 3-5 pm with generally movement to the \nwest northwest into this evening. Main threat from any storm \nwill be strong gusty winds, brief heavy rain and blowing dust.\n\nEnough moisture will be around for the next 7 days for daily\nchances of showers and thunderstorms with day-to-day variability\non areal coverage of storms. \n\nHigh temperatures so far this afternoon have been in the upper\n90s east to the 109 lower deserts. Extreme Heat Warning remains\nin effect until 8 pm this evening. Slightly cooler tomorrow \nwith above normal high temperatures continuing all next week \nwith the end of next week seeing highs like we have seen \nyesterday and today.",
